EPISTLE OF BARNABAS

CH1

21
Thus let us also become like the children of the new covenant lest we become as those who from the beginning heard the word only and enriched themselves.

20
Let us never be found as the hypocrites of whom the scripture says woe to those who lead many astray and lead themselves astray.

19
For it is written as the Spirit says to Him turning to Me from the nations and I will make you as fourteen thousands.

18
Let us never be found as the hypocrites of whom the scripture says woe to those who lead many astray and lead themselves astray.

17
Let us not be like the sinners and wicked men who hear the word only but do not do it.

16
Let us not be as those concerning whom it is written that when they heard the word they immediately went astray and returned to their own bond.

15
Since therefore we live in these things it is not necessary for us to pay attention to men but to God.

14
Thus also when we hear the word let us not enrich ourselves only but become doers of His works.

13
Let us then become spiritual a perfect temple to God.

12
Let us therefore become a perfect temple to God without wavering and blameless.

11
Therefore beloved in these things we give rest to the Holy Spirit because the Lord is good.

10
Blessed are those who have become wise through the Lord because they have known His commandments.

9
Therefore I did not hesitate to counsel you concerning these things so that you also may be saved together.

8
Let us not be as children of the covenant who are disciples of the present time only but also disciples of the Lord.

7
Let us therefore become perfect a perfect temple to God without wavering and blameless.

6
Without wavering and blameless, not being drawn away by our own fleshly lust.

5
Since therefore we are partakers of the covenant let us also become perfect a perfect temple to God.

4
Therefore in these things we give rest to the Holy Spirit because the Lord is good.

3
Therefore I also did not hesitate to counsel you concerning these things so that you also may be saved together.

2
I rejoice and am exceedingly glad concerning your faith and the virtue of the spiritual grace that is in you.

1
Greetings sons and daughters in the name of the Lord who loved us in peace.
